n & rate limiting track** (prevent injection, DoS)\n- **Basic authentication track** (digest/basic auth)\n\nGiven it's a Computer Networks class focusing on networks knowledge, I'd recommend either HTTPS/TLS (deeply network-related) or security headers. Let me suggest TLS/HTTPS as the primary track because it ties directly to networking concepts (handshake, certificates, encryption), with security headers as a secondary layer.\n\n**Prompting tips:**\n- Be specific about language (Go), standard library vs frameworks\n- Ask for modular structure\n- Request comments explaining each part\n- Ask for specific status codes\n- Ask for tests\n- Iterative prompting rather than one big prompt\n- Specify \"educational/simple\" not production-grade\n- Ask for README with how to run\n\nLet me write this up clearly.",
